        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-03T11:06:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This scheme seems difficult to follow. Is it only needed because you want the code to exit early, without doing jniCheck, prepareStatusIntent and agentConnect? If so, it seems like the code would be a lot easier to read (and simpler, too) by using mocks instead.\n\nSpecifically: if you use dummy0 or lo, jniCheck will succeed. After that, the test already mocks out ConnectivityManager, so maybe all it takes is to call:\n\n    verify(mConnectivityManager, timeout(...)).registerNetworkAgent(any(), any(), ...);\n\nI don\u0027t know if making the PendingIntent needs to be mocked or faked but even if it does it should be easy.\n\nIf you don\u0027t do this, add a comments to explain how the CyclicBarrier code works (and specificallly, what events happen in what order). Right now this information is partial and spread across a couple of places.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1195,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1210,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "2e0f165b4339b1f0bd8928ae65eca0c64fd7a9b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c02715a2_2892ebf5",
        "filename": "tests/net/java/com/android/server/connectivity/VpnTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-04T07:44:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mostly it was to wait for the configuration to be done before I can check for the throw route to be installed. But also yes, I wanted to unbranch before jniCheck (jniCheck will crash the test as the native lib is not included in the test (not even caught because Error not Exception), and I didn\u0027t want to add the native lib to the test as it\u0027s a bit more complex than a simple line to the build file (have to deal with variants)).\n\nChanged this based on your suggestion with mocking. Now jniCheck is a dependency, registerNetworkAgent will unblock the test and that lets me do it with a much simpler ConditionVariable. Let me know what you think.",
      "parentUuid": "554118e9_b3f2f65c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1195,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1210,
        "endChar": 0
